"1\n00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,529\nThe Learning Brain. Series 5: Belonging\n\n2\n00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,235\nEpisode 1\n\n3\n00:00:07,315 --> 00:00:09,219\nDo I belong here?\n\n4\n00:00:12,019 --> 00:00:15,332\nPicture two new students who each fail their first quiz.\n\n5\n00:00:15,681 --> 00:00:18,185\nOne thinks, everyone struggles at first.\n\n6\n00:00:18,581 --> 00:00:21,581\nThe other thinks, maybe people like me don't belong here.\n\n7\n00:00:21,938 --> 00:00:23,773\nSame event, different story.\n\n8\n00:00:23,946 --> 00:00:26,435\nAnd the story can shape what happens next.\n\n9\n00:00:26,605 --> 00:00:29,634\nPsychologists call this belonging uncertainty.\n\n10\n00:00:30,041 --> 00:00:31,765\nWhen students aren't sure they fit,\n\n11\n00:00:32,037 --> 00:00:35,918\neveryday setbacks, like a low grade or a cold remark,\n\n12\n00:00:36,075 --> 00:00:37,450\ncan feel like proof.\n\n13\n00:00:37,937 --> 00:00:42,355\nThe worry is more common for students whose group is under represented,\n\n14\n00:00:42,452 --> 00:00:45,414\nor negatively stereotyped, in that setting.\n\n15\n00:00:45,584 --> 00:00:46,774\nIn a classic study,\n\n16\n00:00:47,006 --> 00:00:53,088\nresearchers tested a one hour exercise with ninety two first year students at a selective university.\n\n17\n00:00:53,599 --> 00:01:00,133\nStudents read surveys and stories from older students: worries about belonging were common at first,\n\n18\n00:01:00,377 --> 00:01:01,700\nand faded with time.\n\n19\n00:01:02,275 --> 00:01:05,044\nThen they wrote an essay and gave a short speech,\n\n20\n00:01:05,064 --> 00:01:06,128\nin their own words,\n\n21\n00:01:06,148 --> 00:01:07,409\nfor future students.\n\n22\n00:01:07,579 --> 00:01:09,106\nOver the next three years,\n\n23\n00:01:09,255 --> 00:01:13,190\nthe exercise raised the grades of the African American students,\n\n24\n00:01:13,436 --> 00:01:16,913\nand cut their achievement gap with white students by about half.\n\n25\n00:01:17,558 --> 00:01:19,563\nThey also reported better health,\n\n26\n00:01:19,691 --> 00:01:21,223\nand fewer doctor visits.\n\n27\n00:01:21,562 --> 00:01:22,750\nAnd in senior year,\n\n28\n00:01:22,896 --> 00:01:26,551\nthey showed no awareness that the exercise had made a difference.\n\n29\n00:01:26,721 --> 00:01:29,096\nThe message never said college is easy.\n\n30\n00:01:29,234 --> 00:01:29,847\nIt said: struggle is normal,\n\n31\n00:01:30,126 --> 00:01:33,327\nit is shared, and it changes.\n\n32\n00:01:33,705 --> 00:01:36,687\nThat changed how students read their own setbacks.\n\n33\n00:01:36,857 --> 00:01:37,818\nSome caution.\n\n34\n00:01:38,221 --> 00:01:40,715\nThis was one campus and a small sample.\n\n35\n00:01:41,083 --> 00:01:42,618\nLater and larger studies,\n\n36\n00:01:42,638 --> 00:01:44,055\nin the next episode,\n\n37\n00:01:44,227 --> 00:01:47,115\nfound smaller effects that depended on the setting.\n\n38\n00:01:47,562 --> 00:01:51,707\nA message cannot replace a course that actually welcomes students.\n\n39\n00:01:51,877 --> 00:01:52,661\nFor teaching.\n\n40\n00:01:53,040 --> 00:01:53,963\nEarly in the term,\n\n41\n00:01:53,983 --> 00:01:56,581\ntell students that most people find the start hard,\n\n42\n00:01:56,601 --> 00:01:58,000\nand that it gets better.\n\n43\n00:01:58,423 --> 00:02:00,206\nShare stories from former students,\n\n44\n00:02:00,226 --> 00:02:01,867\nincluding students like them.\n\n45\n00:02:02,199 --> 00:02:05,088\nHave students write advice to next year's class.\n\n46\n00:02:05,396 --> 00:02:07,953\nAnd respond to early setbacks as normal,\n\n47\n00:02:07,995 --> 00:02:08,971\nnot as a verdict.\n\n48\n00:02:09,556 --> 00:02:11,454\nOne tip to share with students: early struggles are normal,\n\n49\n00:02:11,715 --> 00:02:14,364\nand they pass.\n\n50\n00:02:14,534 --> 00:02:17,038\nBelonging isn't a trait students have or lack.\n\n51\n00:02:17,479 --> 00:02:18,545\nIt is a story,\n\n52\n00:02:18,565 --> 00:02:20,256\nand stories can change.\n\n"
